Subject: [PATCH] python-setuptools: drop stale python3-pkg-resources dependency

Old feeds (e.g. openwrt-24.10 python-setuptools 80.9.0) declare
  DEPENDS:=+python3 +python3-pkg-resources
but python3-pkg-resources is only built when explicitly selected, and
new feeds (setuptools>=82, 84.0.0, 2026-08-30) deleted the subpackage
entirely. An unselected/missing provider makes opkg reject the
setuptools candidate:

 * pkg_hash_check_unresolved: cannot find dependency python3-pkg-resources
   for python3-setuptools
 * pkg_hash_fetch_best_installation_candidate: ... incompatible with the
   architectures configured

setuptools runtime does not need pkg_resources (removed upstream), so
drop the dependency. On new feeds this hunk no longer matches (already
DEPENDS:=+python3) -- apply with `patch --forward || true` or guard with
grep, then refresh package metadata.

Converted via: quilt new / quilt add / edit / quilt refresh.
Applies to (old feed only): feeds/packages/lang/python/python-setuptools/Makefile

--- a/feeds/packages/lang/python/python-setuptools/Makefile
+++ b/feeds/packages/lang/python/python-setuptools/Makefile
@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@ endef
 define Package/python3-setuptools
 $(call Package/python3-setuptools/Default)
   TITLE:=Fully-featured library to package Python projects
-  DEPENDS:=+python3 +python3-pkg-resources
+  DEPENDS:=+python3
 endef

 define Package/python3-setuptools/description/Default
